  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1120 AM MDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nOne more typical late May/early June type day for Monday with\ntemperatures over the lowlands in the mid 90s to near 100 degrees.\nThere will be a modest low level moisture push to about the\nContinental Divide but will get mixed out most areas during the\nafternoon. The deeper mid/upper moisture is still way out in\neastern TX and it will be tough to draw this into the area until\nlater in the week. Monday could be the first 100 degree day in El\nPaso but for now kept high at 99 degrees with some lower valley \nareas getting above 100. This looks to be the only 100 degree day \nfor awhile as a slow moving upper low moves out of the Baja region\nand across the Borderland. \n\nThe upper low moving NE through the week will draw in at least low\nlevel moisture from the southeast and bring showers and\nthunderstorms to the Sacs Monday but east of the RGV Tue and \nareawide Wed-Fri with the best chances coming Wed. The best\ninstability will come on Wed as well with some decent 0-6km shear. \nCould see some strong to low end severe storms with hail and gusty\nwinds. PW's get to around 1\" Wed as well and some locally heavy\nrain is also a possible result. Storm motions are still 10-15KTS,\nbut some back-building, especially over the Sacs could result in \nthe biggest flooding concern, especially around recent burn scars.\nHigh temperatures will be below normal by about 5-10 degrees \nduring this period. \n\nThe upper low finally moves out for the weekend bringing back dry\nconditions and temps will warm back up towards average.",
